## Start at the top

The Rijksmuseum holds around eight thousand objects across eighty rooms, which is more than anyone takes in on one visit. Most people head straight for the Gallery of Honour on the second floor, and they are right to: Vermeer, Hals, Steen, and at the far end of it Rembrandt's Night Watch.

Go early or go late. The queue thins after three, and the last hour before closing is the quietest the building gets. Buy a timed ticket online before you come, because weekends sell out.

The garden at the back is free and open to anyone, which makes it a good place to sit when your feet have had enough.

